<Base title="The Hungarian Press"
  eyebrow="Arcanum Digitheca, opened 14 September 2026"
  dek="Lika and the Kvarner were administered from Budapest, and this archive's own place strings still say so. The press and the official publications of that administration had never been searched by anyone in this family — and the first afternoon in them produced a number for the tobacco factory, a Žubrinić who kept a bank's cash, and three Kalanj men of Brinje in a casualty list.">

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>What is readable here, and what is not</h3>
      <p><strong>Everything below is a snippet.</strong> Arcanum returns a full-text extract for
      every hit without a subscription and paywalls the page image behind it —
      <em>«You have no active subscription»</em>. <strong>Not one of these documents has been read
      at the page</strong>, and the OCR's own mangling is left in rather than tidied, because a
      cleaned-up quotation would claim a reading that did not happen.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><strong>Nothing here has been added to the tree.</strong> Not one
      of these people is joined to this family by a document. What the search establishes is that
      the names existed, in those towns, at those dates, doing those things — and where to go next.
      <a href={u("/searched/")}>The search register →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {FINDS.map((f) => (
    <section class="blk">
      <h2>{f.head}</h2>
      <p class="lede">{f.lede}</p>
      {f.quotes.map(([cite, text]) => (
        <figure class="doc" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <blockquote class="prose"><em>{text}</em></blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mono dek">{cite}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
      <p style="margin-top:1rem">{f.so}</p>
      <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href={u(f.link[0])}>{f.link[1]} &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>What was searched, and the two zeros</h2>
    <p class="lede">Every query run on 14 September 2026, with its hit count — because the next
    person should be able to see what has been asked and not ask it again.</p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table class="reg">
        <thead><tr><th style="width:60%">Query</th><th>Hits</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{QUERIES.map(([q, n]) => (
          <tr><td class="mono">{q}</td>
            <td class={n === "0" ? "warn mono" : "mono"}>{n}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="note" style="margin-top:1.2rem"><strong>The two zeros are the useful part.</strong>
    <strong>Šumećica</strong> — the hamlet that the American manifests made important, and the
    birthplace of <a href={u("/direct-line/")}>ahnentafel 10</a> — appears <strong>nowhere in the
    Hungarian press</strong>. And <strong>Senj 1943 returns nothing</strong> to this query, which is
    not a silence about the raid: the raid falls under the Italian occupation, after Hungarian
    administration ended, so <strong>this is the wrong press for it</strong> and the right one has
    still to be found. <a href={u("/senj-1943/")}>Senj, 1943 →</a></div>
    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:1rem"><em>«Blazsevics»</em>, the Hungarian spelling, returns
    <strong>2,168</strong> hits and almost every one of them is a modern footballer. It is recorded
    so that nobody spends an evening on it.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
